  "description": "MOXMUK crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C98 H62 Br14 Dy6 N2 O38,6(C2 H3 N1). From the CIF bond table, Dy01 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy02 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy03 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy5 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy6 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.755-3.937 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 103.01-114.26°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy6(μ3-OH)2(H2O)2(NO3)2(3-bb)14]·6CH3CN. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
